This repo is a simple IMAP to Matrix (matrix.org) bot. If you have e-mail accounts you use just for OTP codes, this could be useful for you.

You will need matrix access_token, and to get one simply use this:
curl -X POST https://{matrix_server}/_matrix/client/v3/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "type": "m.login.password",
    "identifier": {
      "type": "m.id.user",
      "user": "your_username"
    },
    "password": "your_password"
  }'


Response will include:
json
{
  "access_token": "syt_xxxxxxxxxx",
  "device_id": "ABCDEFG",
  "user_id": "@your_username:example.com",
  ...
}

It should work on any OS, but for linux (debian/ubuntu) use autoinstall.sh script. Other OS needs manual installation. MySQL, Python3, and thats all.